{"id":"mahabharata-12-217","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":217,"title":"सप्तदशाधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 217 · Bali's teaching on time","summary":{"en":"Indra mocks Bali again for his lost glory, and Bali replies that all beings are carried by time and that grief is of no use. He says that the one who accepts what comes with a steady mind is not shaken.","kn":"ಇಂದ್ರ ಬಲಿಯ ಕಳೆದ ವೈಭವವನ್ನು ಮತ್ತೆ ಅಪಹಾಸ್ಯ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಎಲ್ಲ ಜೀವಿಗಳನ್ನು ಕಾಲ ಒಯ್ಯುತ್ತದೆ, ಶೋಕ ವ್ಯರ್ಥವೆಂದು ಬಲಿ ಉತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಬಂದುದನ್ನು ಸ್ಥಿರ ಮನಸ್ಸಿನಿಂದ ಸ್ವೀಕರಿಸುವವನು ಕದಲುವುದಿಲ್ಲ.","hi":"इन्द्र बलि के खोए वैभव का फिर उपहास करता है, और बलि उत्तर देता है कि सब प्राणी काल से ढोए जाते हैं और शोक व्यर्थ है। जो आए हुए को स्थिर मन से स्वीकारता है वह विचलित नहीं होता।","te":"ఇంద్రుడు బలి కోల్పోయిన వైభవాన్ని మళ్లీ ఎగతాళి చేస్తాడు; అన్ని జీవులను కాలం మోసుకెళ్తుందని, శోకం వ్యర్థమని బలి బదులిస్తాడు. వచ్చినదాన్ని స్థిర మనసుతో స్వీకరించేవాడు కదలడు.","ta":"இந்திரன் பலியின் இழந்த சிறப்பை மீண்டும் ஏளனம் செய்ய, அனைத்து உயிர்களையும் காலம் சுமந்து செல்கிறது, துயரம் பயனற்றது என்று பலி பதிலளிக்கிறான். வருவதை உறுதியான மனத்துடன் ஏற்பவன் அசைவதில்லை.","ml":"നഷ്ടപ്പെട്ട മഹത്ത്വത്തെക്കുറിച്ച് ഇന്ദ്രൻ ബലിയെ വീണ്ടും പരിഹസിക്കുന്നു; എല്ലാ ജീവികളെയും കാലം വഹിക്കുന്നുവെന്നും ദുഃഖം കൊണ്ട് ഫലമില്ലെന്നും ബലി മറുപടി പറയുന്നു. വരുന്നതിനെ ഉറച്ച മനസ്സോടെ സ്വീകരിക്കുന്നവൻ ഇളകുന്നില്ലെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.217; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पुनरेव तु तं शक्रः प्रहसन्निदमब्रवीत् ।\nनिःश्वसन्तं यथा नागं प्रव्याहाराय भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Indra, laughing, spoke again to Bali, who was hissing like a snake, to draw a reply from him, Bharata."}},{"n":2,"text":"यत्तद्यानसहस्रेण ज्ञातिभिः परिवारितः ।\nलोकान्प्रतापयन्सर्वान्यास्यस्मानवितर्कयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'You who once went in a thousand chariots, surrounded by kin, scorching all the worlds and heeding us not,"}},{"n":3,"text":"दृष्ट्वा सुकृपणां चेमामवस्थामात्मनो बले ।\nज्ञातिमित्रपरित्यक्तः शोचस्याहो न शोचसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"seeing this pitiable state of yours, in your pride of strength, abandoned by kin and friends: do you grieve, or not?'"}},{"n":4,"text":"प्रीतिं प्राप्यातुलां पूर्वं लोकांश्चात्मवशे स्थितान् ।\nविनिपातमिमं चाद्य शोचस्याहो न शोचसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Having once had matchless delight and the worlds under your command, do you today grieve over this fall, or not?'"}},{"text":"बलिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bali said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"अनित्यमुपलक्ष्येदं कालपर्यायमात्मनः ।\nतस्माच्छक्र न शोचामि सर्वं ह्येवेदमन्तवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see that this is impermanent, a turn of time for oneself; therefore, Indra, I do not grieve, for all this has an end."}},{"n":6,"text":"अन्तवन्त इमे देहा भूतानाममराधिप ।\nतेन शक्र न शोचामि नापराधादिदं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bodies of beings end, lord of the immortals; so, Indra, I do not grieve, and this is not from any fault of mine."}},{"n":7,"text":"जीवितं च शरीरं च प्रेत्य वै सह जायते ।\nउभे सह विवर्धेते उभे सह विनश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Life and body are born together after death; both grow together, and both perish together."}},{"n":8,"text":"तदीदृशमिदं भावमवशः प्राप्य केवलम् ।\nयद्येवमभिजानामि का व्यथा मे विजानतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having helplessly come to such a state, if I understand it so, what pain can I have, knowing?"}},{"n":9,"text":"भूतानां निधनं निष्ठा स्रोतसामिव सागरः ।\nनैतत्सम्यग्विजानन्तो नरा मुह्यन्ति वज्रभृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The death of beings is their end, as the sea is the end of rivers; men who do not rightly understand this are deluded, wielder of the thunderbolt."}},{"n":10,"text":"ये त्वेवं नाभिजानन्ति रजोमोहपरायणाः ।\nते कृच्छ्रं प्राप्य सीदन्ति बुद्धिर्येषां प्रणश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who do not understand it so, given to rajas and delusion, fall into hardship, and their understanding is lost."}},{"n":11,"text":"बुद्धिलाभे हि पुरुषः सर्वं नुदति किल्बिषम् ।\nविपाप्मा लभते सत्त्वं सत्त्वस्थः संप्रसीदति ॥","meaning":{"en":"When understanding is gained, a man throws off all sin; freed of sin he gains sattva, and standing in sattva he is serene."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततस्तु ये निवर्तन्ते जायन्ते वा पुनः पुनः ।\nकृपणाः परितप्यन्ते तेऽनर्थैः परिचोदिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those who turn back, or are born again and again, wretched, are tormented, driven by misfortunes."}},{"n":13,"text":"अर्थसिद्धिमनर्थं च जीवितं मरणं तथा ।\nसुखदुःखफलं चैव न द्वेष्मि न च कामये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Success and misfortune, life and death, and the fruit of pleasure and pain: I neither hate nor desire them."}},{"n":14,"text":"हतं हन्ति हतो ह्येव यो नरो हन्ति कंचन ।\nउभौ तौ न विजानीतो यश्च हन्ति हतश्च यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who kills anyone strikes one already struck; neither understands, the one who kills nor the one who is killed."}},{"n":15,"text":"हत्वा जित्वा च मघवन्यः कश्चित्पुरुषायते ।\nअकर्ता ह्येव भवति कर्ता त्वेव करोति तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever, Maghavan, acts as a man after killing and conquering is in truth a non-doer; it is the doer that does it."}},{"n":16,"text":"को हि लोकस्य कुरुते विनाशप्रभवावुभौ ।\nकृतं हि तत्कृतेनैव कर्ता तस्यापि चापरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For who makes both the destruction and the arising of the world? What is done is done by what was done, and its doer has another behind him."}},{"n":17,"text":"पृथिवी वायुराकाशमापो ज्योतिश्च पञ्चमम् ।\nएतद्योनीनि भूतानि तत्र का परिदेवना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Earth, wind, space, water and fire as the fifth: beings have these as their source; what is there to lament?"}},{"n":18,"text":"महाविद्योऽल्पविद्यश्च बलवान्दुर्बलश्च यः ।\nदर्शनीयो विरूपश्च सुभगो दुर्भगश्च यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One greatly learned or little learned, strong or weak, handsome or ugly, fortunate or unfortunate:"}},{"n":19,"text":"सर्वं कालः समादत्ते गम्भीरः स्वेन तेजसा ।\nतस्मिन्कालवशं प्राप्ते का व्यथा मे विजानतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"time takes all, deep, by its own power; when I have come under the power of time, what pain can I feel, knowing?"}},{"n":20,"text":"दग्धमेवानुदहति हतमेवानुहन्ति च ।\nनश्यते नष्टमेवाग्रे लब्धव्यं लभते नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It burns what is already burnt, kills what is already killed; what is lost is lost first, and a man gets what he is to get."}},{"n":21,"text":"नास्य द्वीपः कुतः पारं नावारः संप्रदृश्यते ।\nनान्तमस्य प्रपश्यामि विधेर्दिव्यस्य चिन्तयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It has no island, so how a far shore? No near shore is seen. Pondering this divine ordinance, I see no end to it."}},{"n":22,"text":"यदि मे पश्यतः कालो भूतानि न विनाशयेत् ।\nस्यान्मे हर्षश्च दर्पश्च क्रोधश्चैव शचीपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"If time did not destroy beings before my eyes, then I would feel joy and pride and anger, lord of Shachi."}},{"n":23,"text":"तुषभक्षं तु मां ज्ञात्वा प्रविविक्तजने गृहे ।\nबिभ्रतं गार्दभं रूपमादिश्य परिगर्हसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing me as a husk-eater, living in a house away from people, wearing a donkey's form, you reproach me."}},{"n":24,"text":"इच्छन्नहं विकुर्यां हि रूपाणि बहुधात्मनः ।\nविभीषणानि यानीक्ष्य पलायेथास्त्वमेव मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I wished, I could take many forms of myself, seeing which, terrifying, you would flee from me."}},{"n":25,"text":"कालः सर्वं समादत्ते कालः सर्वं प्रयच्छति ।\nकालेन विधृतं सर्वं मा कृथाः शक्र पौरुषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Time takes everything, time gives everything; all is upheld by time. Do not make a show of manhood, Indra."}},{"n":26,"text":"पुरा सर्वं प्रव्यथते मयि क्रुद्धे पुरंदर ।\nअवैमि त्वस्य लोकस्य धर्मं शक्र सनातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once, when I was angry, everything trembled, Purandara. I know the eternal law of this world, Indra."}},{"n":27,"text":"त्वमप्येवमपेक्षस्व मात्मना विस्मयं गमः ।\nप्रभवश्च प्रभावश्च नात्मसंस्थः कदाचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"You too should look on it so; do not be amazed at yourself. Birth and power never rest in oneself."}},{"n":28,"text":"कौमारमेव ते चित्तं तथैवाद्य यथा पुरा ।\nसमवेक्षस्व मघवन्बुद्धिं विन्दस्व नैष्ठिकीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your mind is still that of a boy, just as it was before. Look carefully, Maghavan, and gain a settled understanding."}},{"n":29,"text":"देवा मनुष्याः पितरो गन्धर्वोरगराक्षसाः ।\nआसन्सर्वे मम वशे तत्सर्वं वेत्थ वासव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gods, men, ancestors, Gandharvas, serpents and rakshasas were all under my power; you know all that, Indra."}},{"n":30,"text":"नमस्तस्यै दिशेऽप्यस्तु यस्यां वैरोचनो बलिः ।\nइति मामभ्यपद्यन्त बुद्धिमात्सर्यमोहिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Homage to that quarter in which Bali son of Virochana lives': so they came to me, their minds clouded by envy and delusion."}},{"n":31,"text":"नाहं तदनुशोचामि नात्मभ्रंशं शचीपते ।\nएवं मे निश्चिता बुद्धिः शास्तुस्तिष्ठाम्यहं वशे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not grieve for that, nor for my own fall, lord of Shachi. Thus my resolve is fixed, and I abide under the ruler."}},{"n":32,"text":"दृश्यते हि कुले जातो दर्शनीयः प्रतापवान् ।\nदुःखं जीवन्सहामात्यो भवितव्यं हि तत्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man born into a good family, handsome and mighty, is seen living in misery with his ministers; it must be so."}},{"n":33,"text":"दौष्कुलेयस्तथा मूढो दुर्जातः शक्र दृश्यते ।\nसुखं जीवन्सहामात्यो भवितव्यं हि तत्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"And one of low family, foolish and ill-born, is seen living happily with his ministers; it must be so."}},{"n":34,"text":"कल्याणी रूपसंपन्ना दुर्भगा शक्र दृश्यते ।\nअलक्षणा विरूपा च सुभगा शक्र दृश्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A beautiful woman, well-formed, is seen unlucky, Indra; and one without good marks and ugly is seen fortunate."}},{"n":35,"text":"नैतदस्मत्कृतं शक्र नैतच्छक्र त्वया कृतम् ।\nयत्त्वमेवंगतो वज्रिन्यद्वाप्येवंगता वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither I nor you, Indra, have brought this about, that you are as you are, wielder of the thunderbolt, and that we are as we are."}},{"n":36,"text":"न कर्म तव नान्येषां कुतो मम शतक्रतो ।\nऋद्धिर्वाप्यथ वा नर्द्धिः पर्यायकृतमेव तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is not your action nor others'; how then mine, Shatakratu? Prosperity or its lack comes only by turn of time."}},{"n":37,"text":"पश्यामि त्वा विराजन्तं देवराजमवस्थितम् ।\nश्रीमन्तं द्युतिमन्तं च गर्जन्तं च ममोपरि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see you shining, established as king of the gods, glorious and radiant, roaring over me."}},{"n":38,"text":"एतच्चैवं न चेत्कालो मामाक्रम्य स्थितो भवेत् ।\nपातयेयमहं त्वाद्य सवज्रमपि मुष्टिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"If time did not stand over me, mastering me, I would strike you down today with my fist, thunderbolt and all."}},{"n":39,"text":"न तु विक्रमकालोऽयं क्षमाकालोऽयमागतः ।\nकालः स्थापयते सर्वं कालः पचति वै तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"But this is not the time for prowess; the time for forbearance has come. Time sets everything, and time ripens everything."}},{"n":40,"text":"मां चेदभ्यागतः कालो दानवेश्वरमूर्जितम् ।\nगर्जन्तं प्रतपन्तं च कमन्यं नागमिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"If time has come upon me, a mighty lord of the Danavas, roaring and blazing, whom will it not come upon?"}},{"n":41,"text":"द्वादशानां हि भवतामादित्यानां महात्मनाम् ।\nतेजांस्येकेन सर्वेषां देवराज हृतानि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"King of the gods, I once took away, by myself, the radiance of all you twelve great Adityas."}},{"n":42,"text":"अहमेवोद्वहाम्यापो विसृजामि च वासव ।\nतपामि चैव त्रैलोक्यं विद्योताम्यहमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"I alone bore the waters and let them go, Vasava; I alone burned the three worlds and I alone made them shine."}},{"n":43,"text":"संरक्षामि विलुम्पामि ददाम्यहमथाददे ।\nसंयच्छामि नियच्छामि लोकेषु प्रभुरीश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I guarded, I plundered, I gave, I took; I restrained and I controlled, lord and master in the worlds."}},{"n":44,"text":"तदद्य विनिवृत्तं मे प्रभुत्वममराधिप ।\nकालसैन्यावगाढस्य सर्वं न प्रतिभाति मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"That sovereignty of mine has now turned away, lord of the immortals; plunged in time's army, nothing appears to me."}},{"n":45,"text":"नाहं कर्ता न चैव त्वं नान्यः कर्ता शचीपते ।\nपर्यायेण हि भुज्यन्ते लोकाः शक्र यदृच्छया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither I am the doer, nor you, nor anyone else, lord of Shachi; the worlds are enjoyed in turn, Indra, by chance."}},{"n":46,"text":"मासार्धमासवेश्मानमहोरात्राभिसंवृतम् ।\nऋतुद्वारं वर्षमुखमाहुर्वेदविदो जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who know the Veda say that the year has half-months and months as its house, is wrapped in days and nights, with seasons as its doors and the rains as its face."}},{"n":47,"text":"आहुः सर्वमिदं चिन्त्यं जनाः केचिन्मनीषया ।\nअस्याः पञ्चैव चिन्तायाः पर्येष्यामि च पञ्चधा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some people say all this is to be considered by thought; I will examine this thought in five and in five ways."}},{"n":48,"text":"गम्भीरं गहनं ब्रह्म महत्तोयार्णवं यथा ।\nअनादिनिधनं चाहुरक्षरं परमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahman is deep and dense like a great ocean of water; they call it without beginning or end, imperishable and supreme."}},{"n":49,"text":"सत्त्वेषु लिङ्गमावेश्य नलिङ्गमपि तत्स्वयम् ।\nमन्यन्ते ध्रुवमेवैनं ये नरास्तत्त्वदर्शिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having entered into beings by a mark, though itself without mark: those who see the truth hold it to be constant."}},{"n":50,"text":"भूतानां तु विपर्यासं मन्यते गतवानिति ।\nन ह्येतावद्भवेद्गम्यं न यस्मात्प्रकृतेः परः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He thinks of the change of beings as 'gone'; but this is not all that can be reached, for there is nothing beyond nature."}},{"n":51,"text":"गतिं हि सर्वभूतानामगत्वा क्व गमिष्यसि ।\nयो धावता न हातव्यस्तिष्ठन्नपि न हीयते ।\nतमिन्द्रियाणि सर्वाणि नानुपश्यन्ति पञ्चधा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not having gone to the end of all beings, where will you go? That which cannot be left by one who runs and is not lost though standing, the senses do not see in five ways."}},{"n":52,"text":"आहुश्चैनं केचिदग्निं केचिदाहुः प्रजापतिम् ।\nऋतुमासार्धमासांश्च दिवसांस्तु क्षणांस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some call it fire, some Prajapati, the season, month, half-month, days and moments."}},{"n":53,"text":"पूर्वाह्णमपराह्णं च मध्याह्नमपि चापरे ।\nमुहूर्तमपि चैवाहुरेकं सन्तमनेकधा ।\nतं कालमवजानीहि यस्य सर्वमिदं वशे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others call it forenoon, afternoon and midday, and a muhurta: though one, they speak of it as many. Know that as Time, in whose power all this is."}},{"n":54,"text":"बहूनीन्द्रसहस्राणि समतीतानि वासव ।\nबलवीर्योपपन्नानि यथैव त्वं शचीपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many thousands of Indras have passed, Vasava, endowed with strength and valour just as you are, lord of Shachi."}},{"n":55,"text":"त्वामप्यतिबलं शक्रं देवराजं बलोत्कटम् ।\nप्राप्ते काले महावीर्यः कालः संशमयिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even you, Indra, king of the gods, very strong and proud in strength, when the time comes mighty Time will quell."}},{"n":56,"text":"य इदं सर्वमादत्ते तस्माच्छक्र स्थिरो भव ।\nमया त्वया च पूर्वैश्च न स शक्योऽतिवर्तितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who takes all this: therefore, Indra, be steady. He cannot be escaped by me, by you, or by those before."}},{"n":57,"text":"यामेतां प्राप्य जानीषे राजश्रियमनुत्तमाम् ।\nस्थिता मयीति तन्मिथ्या नैषा ह्येकत्र तिष्ठति ॥","meaning":{"en":"That supreme royal fortune you now have, which you think stays with you: that is false, for it does not stay in one place."}},{"n":58,"text":"स्थिता हीन्द्रसहस्रेषु त्वद्विशिष्टतमेष्वियम् ।\nमां च लोला परित्यज्य त्वामगाद्विबुधाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"It has stayed with thousands of Indras, better than you; and fickle, it left me and went to you, lord of the gods."}},{"n":59,"text":"मैवं शक्र पुनः कार्षीः शान्तो भवितुमर्हसि ।\nत्वामप्येवंगतं त्यक्त्वा क्षिप्रमन्यं गमिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do not act like this again, Indra; you should be calm. Leaving you too, in such a state, it will soon go to another."}}]}]}